 "about": "The pieces of SwiftUI Quest that are implementation details, by their id in quest.json. library/quest.js gives every step, sheet section, flash card, edge case, and interview problem implementation: true when its id is here, and false otherwise. A piece is an implementation detail when what it teaches is what Swift, a macro, the runtime, or SwiftUI makes or keeps for the code, and not the code you write and what it does: the code that swiftc or a macro writes, such as an expansion, a synthesized conformance, or the hidden storage of a wrapped property; SIL, LLVM IR, or the source of the standard library, the compiler, or SwiftUI; the real types that SwiftUI builds, such as ModifiedContent; memory layout and sizes; threads, queues, and executors; and SwiftUI's own updates, such as when it compares a view. A rule that Apple documents and a program shows from the outside, such as when body runs or how layout sizes a view, is not. These were judged by reading each piece, after a search for words such as SIL, expansion, and ModifiedContent found the candidates.",
